{"title":"Career Roadmap · Safety Auditor","role":"Safety Auditor","summary":"A Safety Auditor evaluates whether workplaces, facilities, processes and safety-management systems comply with applicable safety requirements, internal standards and good practices. The role can involve site inspections, hazard identification, fire-safety assessment, industrial-process review, documentation, corrective-action tracking and audit reporting.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starting point"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Fire & Industrial Safety"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Safety Auditor"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Occupational Safety · Fire Safety · Industrial HSE"}],[{"text":"Primary work"},{"text":"Inspections + audits + hazard assessment + reporting"}],[{"text":"Core capability"},{"text":"Risk identification + regulatory compliance"}],[{"text":"Important technical skill"},{"text":"Fire/process/workplace safety"}],[{"text":"Important professional skill"},{"text":"Report writing + communication"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build industrial safety, fire safety, risk assessment and emergency-response fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in HSE audits, process safety, fire safety, construction safety or environmental compliance"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Progress toward Senior Safety Auditor, HSE Specialist, Lead Auditor or Safety Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Lead integrated safety systems using digital monitoring, predictive risk analytics and process-safety technology"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc in Fire & Industrial Safety, the most realistic progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.S